  "id": "COMPOUND:23337 - PROTEIN:4718",
  "verbalization": "Nanolobatin B appears to have multiple targets that ultimately converge on Myosin light chain kinase 3, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Nanolobatin B acts as a target for several compounds, including (3S,4S,5S)-3-[(Z)-Hexadec-7-Enyl]-4-Hydroxy-5-Methyloxolan-2-One, 1-O-beta-D-Glucopyranosyl anthranilate, and Bullatine A, all of which are linked to Myosin light chain kinase 3. These targets may share common mechanisms of action, such as modulating signaling pathways or influencing protein interactions, which could explain the observed relationship. The integration of these pathways suggests that Nanolobatin B may exert its effects through a series of molecular intermediates that ultimately target Myosin light chain kinase 3, potentially through a mechanism involving receptor activation or enzyme inhibition. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on Myosin light chain kinase 3 supports the hypothesis that Nanolobatin B may act as a modulator of this kinase, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
